00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:07,700
Well, Charlie and I were talking, and...

263
00:16:10,067 --> 00:16:11,227
You kissed.

264
00:16:11,230 --> 00:16:14,690
Wh-- What?

265
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:20,540
What? What would give you that idea?

266
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:22,460
- I saw you.  - Yeah, we kissed.

267
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:27,240
But nothing else.

268
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,760
Nothing else happened, okay?

269
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:31,820
- Ross...It's okay.  - What?

270
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:41,226
It's okay. You know, look l totally understand, all right? You guys make way more sense than her and I ever did, you know?

271
00:16:41,246 --> 00:16:42,106
And....

272
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:45,960
- I want you to be happy. - Are you serious?

273
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:47,340
Yeah.

274
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:53,280
- Now I have something--  - I am speechless.

275
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:59,560
I mean, the fact that you would put my happiness first like that, I mean....

276
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:02,220
You're an incredible friend, do you know that?

277
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:05,240
- Well, look, before you go--  - No, I mean it.

278
00:17:05,840 --> 00:17:08,198
I mean, you're so loyal, man.

279
00:17:08,218 --> 00:17:12,538
And selfless and generous.

280
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,820
I am those things, yeah.

281
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:24,980
I've known Chandler longer, so I think of him as my best friend. But now l may have to rethink some stuff.

282
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:27,000
Dude!

283
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:31,800
Hey, if there is ever anything I can do for you....

284
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:35,520
I can't think of anything.

285
00:17:38,722 --> 00:17:40,572
- Thanks.  - Yeah.

286
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:46,320
- So hi.  - Hi.

287
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:47,980
So you talked to Joey?

288
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:51,100
Oh, yeah. We had a really good talk.

289
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,820
- Oh, that's great.  - Yeah.

290
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:54,260
So everything's okay?

291
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,860
Oh, no, it's great.

292
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:58,700
It's great. He's an amazing guy.

293
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:01,760
Oh, well, obviously, I think so too.

294
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,780
Well, I'm so excited about this.

295
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:08,660
Really? Excited?

296
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:10,840
What, are you kidding?

297
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:14,640
I have had some very dirty dreams about this.

298
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:18,960
Excuse me.

299
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:28,440
You didn't tell him, did you?

300
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:29,580
I couldn't.

301
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:32,240
He was saying all these really nice things about me.

302
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:34,280
I didn't want him to get mad and take them back.

303
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:35,340
I'm gonna edge out Chandler!

304
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:38,900
Fine. Yon know what Joey. Forget it.

305
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:40,660
When we go back to New York, I will tell him.

306
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,720
Thank you. Yeah, I appreciate that.

307
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:04,680
- Hi, Mike's place.  - Hey, it's Mike.

308
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:07,820
- That was fast.  - Oh, no, she's not here yet.

309
00:19:08,660 --> 00:19:12,100
You know, I'm just gonna take off and break up with her over the phone.

310
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:14,540
You can't do that. Oh, come on,

311
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:15,860
Mike, strap on a pair.

312
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:20,600
Why don't you tell her that we got back together.

313
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:22,460
You know, women appreciate honesty.

314
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:27,080
We also appreciate gentle spanking once in a while, just FYl.

315
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,320
One more thing.

316
00:19:31,160 --> 00:19:34,120
There might be a picture of Precious on my coffee table.

317
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:35,500
Her name's Precious?

318
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:39,060
Is she a pure breed, or did you pick her up at the pound?

319
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:43,000
Any way, I just want to give you a heads up.

320
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,220
Okay. And if she gets upset.

321
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:47,600
...just scratch her tummy and give her a liver snap.

322
00:19:57,940 --> 00:19:59,580
Hi. I'm Precious. Who are you?

323
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,000
- I'm Phoebe.  - Phoebe?

324
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:05,200
Mike's ex-girlfriend, Phoebe?

325
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:07,240
The love of his life? That Phoebe?

326
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:16,720
Oh, I can't wait for everyone at work to see these!

327
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,600
You go back to work tomorrow night?

328
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:21,560
Yeah.

329
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:26,440
So if you want people to see them you're not having them taken out, say, at the break of dawn?

330
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:31,180
Well, if I had them taken out, then I wouldn't be able to do this.

331
00:20:38,020 --> 00:20:39,180
You like that, right?

332
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:48,280
What are you singing?

333
00:20:48,365 --> 00:20:50,525
It's "Bolero" from <i>10.</i>

334
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:53,520
It's "Ride of the Valkyries" from <i>Apocalypse Now.</i>

335
00:20:55,300 --> 00:20:58,660
Here's the thing. The cornrows were a solution to your frizzy-hair problem.

336
00:20:58,980 --> 00:21:00,700
Now that we're home, you don't have that problem.

337
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,260
If you think about it...

338
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:03,500
I hate them.

339
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:07,380
What? You said you liked them.

340
00:21:07,520 --> 00:21:09,180
Did l? Let's refresh.

341
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:12,060
I believe what I said was that I could see your scalp.

342
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:15,480
Well, fine. So you don't like them.

343
00:21:15,740 --> 00:21:16,620
Everybody else does.

344
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:19,400
Again, let's journey back.

345
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:24,800
As I recall, Rachel said she had never noticed the shape of your skull before.

346
00:21:25,908 --> 00:21:27,338
And Joey?

347
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:29,560
Well, Joey didn't realize there was anything different.

348
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:32,160
You know what? I don't care.

349
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:34,260
I like it like this, and I'm gonna keep it.

350
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:36,780
You're just jealous because your hair can't do this.

351
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:43,500
- Get yourself in the tooth? - And the eye.

352
00:21:53,560 --> 00:21:56,220
Hi! There she is! Hi, Emma.

353
00:21:56,260 --> 00:21:58,440
Oh, my God, I missed you.

354
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:01,460
Oh, Emma, I missed you so much. Hi.

355
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,940
Did you have a good time with Grandma Green? Huh?

356
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:08,500
Did she give you a bottle of antidepressants again to use as a rattle?

357
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:13,940
That was one time, Ross, and they were only, like, five milligrams.

358
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:18,800
Hey, Emma, Daddy has some presents for you, okay?

359
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:20,400
I want you to wait right here.

360
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:21,500
Come here, sweetie.

361
00:22:24,200 --> 00:22:26,100
Ross, actually, there's something that

362
00:22:26,380 --> 00:22:27,940
I really need to talk to you about.

363
00:22:28,020 --> 00:22:28,640
Okay, shoot.

364
00:22:29,858 --> 00:22:35,668
- Okay. All right, here's the deal.  - Oh, no!

365
00:22:36,780 --> 00:22:37,540
What is it?

366
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:40,760
Oh, major shampoo explosion!

367
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:44,980
Look, Ross, this really isn't easy.

368
00:22:45,020 --> 00:22:46,800
Oh, it's all over everything!

369
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:51,740
Why? Why me?

370
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:55,540
Because you took 300 bottles of shampoo?

371
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:59,900
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. You were saying?

372
00:23:00,460 --> 00:23:03,040
Well, yeah. Look, it's about me and--

373
00:23:03,060 --> 00:23:05,420
Oh, not another one!

374
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:10,020
Oh, my--Oh, and this is moisturizer!

375
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:11,780
It's even harder to clean!

376
00:23:13,820 --> 00:23:14,220
Why?

377
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:17,200
Why do bad things happen to good people?

378
00:23:19,260 --> 00:23:22,460
Wow. Clearly this is not a good time.

379
00:23:22,746 --> 00:23:23,816
You think?

380
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:28,820
Okay. Bye.

381
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:32,320
All right, so Mike's on his way over.

382
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:36,880
You thought you were meeting here, he thought at the restaurant, so....

383
00:23:37,330 --> 00:23:38,980
It doesn't matter who's right or wrong.

384
00:23:39,100 --> 00:23:41,920
The point is, I'm gonna take off.

385
00:23:43,060 --> 00:23:46,080
Wait. I'm not letting you leave until you tell me what's going on here.

386
00:23:46,080 --> 00:23:48,960
I mean are you guys getting back together or something?

387
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:52,080
All right.

388
00:23:54,820 --> 00:23:56,500
Susie-- Can I call you Susie?

389
00:23:57,820 --> 00:23:59,180
My name is Precious.

390
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:01,820
I can't say that.

391
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:06,400
Susie, I'm gonna be straight with you.

392
00:24:07,300 --> 00:24:09,400
Mike and I are back together.

393
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:15,180
And unfortunately that effectively ends your relationship with him.

394
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:21,500
He's very sorry about that, and wishes you the best luck in all your endeavors.

395
00:24:23,340 --> 00:24:26,400
I just can't believe this. Why?

396
00:24:27,300 --> 00:24:28,400
Well, I don't--

397
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,360
Why would he do this?

398
00:24:29,660 --> 00:24:30,760
What's wrong with me?

399
00:24:31,320 --> 00:24:32,200
There's nothing wrong with you.

400
00:24:32,360 --> 00:24:34,400
What the hell am I supposed to do now?

401
00:24:34,700 --> 00:24:36,940
Damn it, woman! Pull yourself together!

402
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:40,460
Have some pride, for the love of God!

403
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:47,100
Okay, not a fan of the tough love.

404
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:52,480
I just can't believe that Mike didn't give me any warning.

405
00:24:53,100 --> 00:24:53,840
He didn't know.

406
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:57,860
He wasn't planning on coming to Barbados and proposing to me.

407
00:24:58,160 --> 00:24:59,640
He proposed to you?

408
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:02,900
This is the worst birthday ever!

409
00:25:07,495 --> 00:25:09,955
Look, Precious...

410
00:25:12,760 --> 00:25:14,100
Mike's not worth this.

411
00:25:14,400 --> 00:25:18,940
You're an attractive intelligent woman and let's face it, Mike's kind of a wang.

412
00:25:20,480 --> 00:25:22,960
He proposed to me while he was still seeing you.

413
00:25:23,380 --> 00:25:25,900
He was gonna break up with you on your birthday?

414
00:25:26,920 --> 00:25:30,840
I don't like to kiss and tell, but he cheated on you a lot this weekend.

415
00:25:31,440 --> 00:25:33,200
Oh, my God, you know, maybe you're right.

416
00:25:33,460 --> 00:25:34,680
Maybe I don't need him.

417
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:37,060
I deserve to be treated with respect.

418
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:39,800
Screw you, Mike.

419
00:25:40,060 --> 00:25:43,200
You're a coward and a bastard, and I hope you rot in hell!

420
00:25:49,340 --> 00:25:50,260
You're welcome.

421
00:25:56,740 --> 00:25:58,700
Honey? You've been in there for a long time.

422
00:25:58,760 --> 00:25:59,680
Is everything okay?

423
00:26:00,900 --> 00:26:01,700
Not really.

424
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:06,240
I have a problem.

425
00:26:07,820 --> 00:26:10,220
Really? What happened?

426
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:19,400
Well, I was dancing around and singing "No Woman, No Cry"  and I got stuck.

427
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:22,280
You can't move at all?

428
00:26:22,480 --> 00:26:23,720
Oh, I can move.

429
00:26:30,500 --> 00:26:33,520
If I untangle you, will you please get rid of the cornrows?

430
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:34,840
I guess so.

431
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:38,900
Some of these look a little frayed.

432
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:41,440
Yeah, I tried to gnaw myself free.

433
00:26:45,920 --> 00:26:47,080
- Hey. - Hi.

434
00:26:47,520 --> 00:26:53,800
- So? Did you tell Ross?  - Well, I tried but then he had a shampoo-related emergency.

435
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:57,240
- So I guess now it's your turn again.  - No...

436
00:26:58,060 --> 00:26:59,660
I think it's better if you tell him.

437
00:26:59,850 --> 00:27:01,480
You know, it's easier for a woman.

438
00:27:01,880 --> 00:27:04,240
That way, you know, if he gets mad, all you have to do is go

439
00:27:04,600 --> 00:27:07,680
I didn't mean it.

440
00:27:08,500 --> 00:27:10,300
I'm so sorry

441
00:27:14,520 --> 00:27:15,720
Yeah, 'cause that's what we do.

442
00:27:16,800 --> 00:27:20,700
Alright, alright, okay, uhm... How about this? Tomorrow...

443
00:27:22,280 --> 00:27:24,860
Tomorrow we'll both go and we'll tell him together.

444
00:27:25,960 --> 00:27:27,160
Okay, that sounds fair.

445
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:29,460
That just means, once again, we can't--

446
00:27:29,480 --> 00:27:30,360
I know...

447
00:27:30,500 --> 00:27:31,280
That's okay.

448
00:27:31,940 --> 00:27:33,840
I mean, we can control ourselves.

449
00:27:33,900 --> 00:27:34,440
We're not animals.

450
00:27:34,760 --> 00:27:37,560
- No! Of course, we can wait.  - Yeah.

451
00:27:39,700 --> 00:27:41,760
All right, so I guess that means good night then.

452
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,800
Yep. Good night.

453
00:27:51,106 --> 00:27:52,136
Good night.

454
00:27:54,260 --> 00:27:55,740
Good night.

455
00:28:02,300 --> 00:28:03,840
Seriously, good night.

456
00:28:03,840 --> 00:28:04,740
Stop saying good night.

457
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:27,940
I'm so sorry.

458
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:37,860
Look what I found in the drawer.

459
00:28:40,700 --> 00:28:42,900
And you said I'd never wear this.

460
00:28:44,580 --> 00:28:48,200
Now that I untangled you, how about you do a little something for me?

461
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:50,020
Sure. What did you have in mind?

462
00:28:50,540 --> 00:28:51,640
I think you know.

463
00:28:52,380 --> 00:28:54,700
Really? I don't-- I don't really feel like it.

464
00:28:54,980 --> 00:28:56,900
This is what I want to do.

465
00:28:58,700 --> 00:28:59,220
Okay.

466
00:28:59,700 --> 00:29:02,300
I just don't get why you like it so much.

467
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:07,380
She's a FBI agent, posing as a beauty contestant.

